Task #858: Unify admin detection across sidebar and route guards

Original task: make the dashboard sidebar and the AdminRoute /
ProtectedRoute admin gate read admin status from a single shared source
so they cannot disagree (the split-brain bug Task #856 set out to fix).

Findings:
- The sidebar (`DashboardLayout.tsx`) already consumes `useIsAdmin` and
  no longer reads `subscription.plan === "admin"` or
  `user.user_metadata.role === "admin"` for admin detection.
- `AdminRoute.tsx` already consumes `useIsAdmin`.
- `ProtectedRoute.tsx`'s `AdminGate` already consumes `useIsAdmin`.
- The contract test `admin-role-detection.test.tsx` already mocks only
  the single `useIsAdmin` hook (not two independent sources), confirming
  the unified source of truth.

Changes in this task:
- Removed a stale comment in `DashboardLayout.tsx` that still referred to
  admin being detected from "user metadata or subscription plan", and
  replaced it with an accurate description of the current single-source
  contract (email allowlist + server-side `has_role` RPC via
  `useIsAdmin`).

Verification:
- `npx vitest run src/__tests__/admin-role-detection.test.tsx` — all 5
  tests pass.

No deviations from task scope. No follow-ups proposed (existing tasks
in the project already cover related work like profile identity
unification).

